BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Yoga-on-the-Lawn-16x9-1.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 023/05/Yoga-on-the-Lawn-16x9-1.jpg
UID:IWK9qAU8kWpve8XeoskoX
SUMMARY:Yoga on the Lawn
DTSTAMP:20260731T055407Z
DTSTART:20260920T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:FREE for members / $15 nonmemberAges 16+\, minors must be accom
	panied by an adult \n\n\n\nJoin us for a grounding yoga practice surrounde
	d by the beautiful sounds and sights of nature! Taught by Carolina Vennie 
	of Yogaleena\, this class will be a Vinyasa Flow that is accessible to all
	 levels. \n\n\n\nPlease bring your own mat and water. This class is weathe
	r dependent and pre-registration is required. \n\n\n\n\nseptember 20\n\n\n
	\noctober 11\n\n\n\nnovember 15\n\n\n\ndecember 13\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIf the
	 event is canceled due to the weather\, paid attendees may attend next mon
	th’s session. No refunds will be given. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor bio: Th
	rough Carolina Vennie’s quirky humor and playful instruction\, you will le
	arn to strengthen your body while relaxing your mind\, increase your flexi
	bility and freedom of movement\, and find that sweet spot between effort a
	nd ease that you can apply on and off the mat. Carolina’s teaching is infl
	uenced by years of practice in Washington D.C. studios and a deep desire t
	o share with others the importance of self-discovery\, exploring your crea
	tivity\, trusting your intuition\, and the life-changing benefits of yoga.
	\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/yoga-on-the-lawn/2026-09-20/\n\nFro
	m Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/yoga-on-the-lawn/2026-09-20/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
